# Bounds the explorer's systemd stdout/stderr logs on the production host
# (spec proactive-system-watch, 2.0.4).
#
# Installs as /etc/logrotate.d/xchain-explorer-app. The name matters: the box
# already has /etc/logrotate.d/xchain-explorer, and that file holds the APACHE
# access-log stanza for /var/log/apache2/explorer/*.log (1-day retention, wallet
# addresses in the request lines, operator decision 2026-08-02). Installing this
# under the bare name would overwrite it and drop the address-log retention
# guarantee.
#
# Nothing rotates these two paths unless a stanza names them, and a deployment
# that assumes otherwise finds out slowly: a per-cycle warning loop (a price
# feed reporting "price unavailable", say) grows stderr.log by hundreds of
# megabytes a month until the filesystem it sits on is threatened. This stanza
# is what stops that.
#
# copytruncate, not create: the unit writes with StandardOutput/StandardError=
# append:, holding one O_APPEND fd per file for the life of the process. A
# rename-and-recreate rotation would leave systemd writing to the unlinked inode
# and the fresh file empty until the next explorer restart, which on a
# Restart=always service could be weeks.
#
# No delaycompress. It exists to protect a rotated file that a process still
# holds open, which is exactly what copytruncate has already ruled out: the copy
# is taken and the original truncated in place, so nothing is reading the
# rotated file by the time compression runs. Driving the first rotation proved
# the cost of keeping both: stderr.log.1 sat at its full uncompressed size and
# the disk pressure this stanza exists to relieve was still there afterwards.
#
# Retention: daily rotation with 7 copies keeps a week, far past the 48 h
# floor a support question needs; maxsize 100M is the ceiling for a fault loop
# that outruns the daily cadence, so a bounded amount of disk is committed
# whatever the log rate turns out to be.
/home/<deploy-user>/xchain-explorer/logs/*.log {
    su <deploy-user> <deploy-user>
    daily
    rotate 7
    maxsize 100M
    missingok
    notifempty
    compress
    copytruncate
}
